In my continuing quest to ascend with every class (and race) on the
NAO server, my elven wizard reached the status of demigoddess early
this morning. While I don't startscum wizards, I was happy to begin
with some decent inventory items, including a scroll of identify and
spellbook of extra healing. An altar on level one, magic lamp in
Izchak's shop, and co-aligned temple in Minetown also helped me get to
a good start. I named Sting and quickly trained dagger to Expert in
anticipation of receiving MagicBane, and used the starting force bolt
spell on enough early monsters to train attack skill to expert as
well.

Though I had some close calls with a pack of winter wolves in the
Mines, judicious use of Elbereth helped me dispatch them and get to
the bones pile of the unfortunate player they previously dismembered.
Nothing terribly remarkable contained therein, but soon a wand of
polymorph turned one of my army of dogs and cats into a nice gray
dragon, who chomped on all shopkeepers (sparing Izchak), allowing me
to max out my protection quickly. Wished-for silver dragon scale mail,
starting cloak of magic resistance, and a bag of holding from Minetown
meant I could once again skip the hated Sokoban.

Despite a good deal of sacrificing at the temple, I was unable to get
a really decent weapon other than Magicbane. Even if I had wanted to
wish for an artifact weapon (which I didn't, as I very rarely violate
that conduct), there were already too many artifacts in the game;
besides Sting, I'd found Mjollnir in that bones pile in the mines (but
it blasted me and I didn't really want to use it anyway) and been
granted Trollsbane (gee thanks). I decided to see if I could win the
game with MB, spells, and pets alone. Enchanting to +2, it seemed to
do well enough against most beasties. Charm monster brought Medusa's
Titan to my side, handy and high on hit points though with a voracious
appetite.

Magic mapping got me through Gehennom quickly. I had been crowned and
so had finger of death, but mostly used cone of cold as it took less
power. I still hadn't found or polypiled magic missile (never found
Ludios so my polypiling was more limited than usual), but didn't want
to waste a wish on it. In Moloch's Sanctum I took enough damage that I
decided to use the Eye to return to my stash in Minetown and re-read
all my spells before the ascension run. I also wrote my own magic
missile spellbook - lucky that worked since I'd never seen one, but
Wizards get a better chance to do so. A few more sacrifices granted me
Werebane, and while it had no special bonus against most monsters I
decided the silver damage would be handy against demons, and I really
wanted to have something besides MB so I enchanted it to +7. With
Rodney on my tail and my curses surrounding my inventory despite
dropping the Book and not having the Amulet yet (is this a bug?), I
wasn't going to hang around for hundreds more turns waiting for Frost
Brand (my favorite besides Grayswandir, which is only for lawfuls).

After doing that, I returned to the high priest's temple to find him
absent, with no Amulet in sight! Frantically I searched the entire
level, thinking back to disintegration blasts from a black dragon (but
the Amulet can't be destroyed, right?), whether Rodney had anything
with him on any of his appearances (he hadn't, and I took him out with
one finger each time), or whether the priest had perhaps level-
teleported out. Finally thinking the last conclusion may unfortunately
be correct, I went up a level, to find Yeenoghu on the upstair. I
remembered him running up there when I beat on him earlier, but didn't
think about the implications at the time. Teleporting to the stair and
taking him out, I finally retrieved the Amulet.

Getting back up was easy. I reunited with my gray dragon in the
Castle; he was surprisingly still tame. I wished for a ring of
conflict as I'd never found one, dumped a bunch of excess inventory,
and left the dungeon. Couldn't get the dragon to go through the portal
to the plane of Air with me, but that was OK; once levitating I was
finally unburdened, and easily eluded the air elementals on the way to
the portal. Took off the ring before entering Astral so I could get my
pet Angel. I tried using the Candelabrum for light and the jumping
spell as I'd read that suggestion, but kept bumping into things. Death
drained off over 50HP as MB and WB weren't terribly effective on him,
as I feared. But I still had nearly 300HP by the end. First altar was
the right one, and I had succeeded with my fifth NAO class and fourth
race. Though unfortunately my score was not high enough to get on the
top 2000 list this time, this was my fastest NAO ascension so far,
though not at all speedy at >64K turns.

